From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0921 redfin: camera capture path, step 1: the CSID test pattern into memory

"c 20" (sweetcam=2): HackiOS redwood_camera.c cam=3 with lito's numbers. The
CSID-lite and IFE-lite register files are the same in both kernels (Titan
17x: cam_ife_csid_lite17x.h, cam_vfe_lite17x.h + vfe bus ver2). lito's:
camcc PLL0 (Lucid, 1200 MHz, cam_cc_pll0_config), RCGs at the DT's lowest
levels (slow_ahb 80, camnoc_axi 150, cphy_rx/csiNphytimer/ife_lite_csid 300,
ife_lite 400 MHz) and their branches, GCC camera hf/sf AXI, mx.lvl at
SVS_L1 (cx.lvl is wland's, at its top); frame memory from the GPU pool
(below 4 GB: the write master's addresses are 32-bit); the IFE streams
(0x800/0x5e0) through an apps-SMMU context bank with translation off, as
phone/wifi/radio.c does for the WLAN. One 1600x1200 RAW10 colour-bar frame
through RDI 0 and write master 0 in frame mode; everything taken back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WuzsiVGCDDmN2GPRLJvX3w
